'''M80''' is an [[:category:United States|American]] esports organization based in [[wikipedia:Boston|Boston, Massachusetts]].

==History==
===Biography===
M80 entered ''VALORANT'' in 2022, signing the core of the ex-[[Ghost Gaming]] roster.<ref name="M80 enters valo">{{cite web|url=https://x.com/M80gg/status/1600913108524232705|title=Spike planted. Your move.|author='''M80'''|date=2022-12-08}}</ref> M80 would go on to compete in Challengers North America; with the organisation qualifying to Ascension in both [[VCL/2023/Ascension/Americas|2023]] and [[VCL/2024/Ascension/Americas|2024]] finishing in second place in both tournaments and thereby missing out on the promotion to the [[VCT]] Americas Partnership league twice.

M80 continued their time in Challengers into 2025, finishing [[VCL/2025/North_America/Stage_1|Stage 1]] in second place. Following the end of the Stage, M80's roster went through some serious changes: assistant coach [[DrewSpark]] left to join [[G2 Gozen]], and [[okeanos]] and [[Sato]] joing [[Leviatán]] in VCT Americas.<ref name="Sato">{{Cite web|url=https://x.com/LeviatanGG/status/1922792785045807436|title=@sato_pequeno se une à equipe para o EWC Americas Qualifier em busca da vaga para o #EWC2025|trans_title=Sato joins the ranks of LEVIATHAN to achieve qualification to EWC 2025|language={{flag|esmx}} Spanish|author='''Leviatán'''|date=2025-05-14}}</ref><ref name="Okeanos">{{Cite web|url=https://x.com/LeviatanGG/status/1922774025400418773|title=@OkeanosQT se suma a las filas de LEVIATÁN para conquistar la clasificación a #EWC2025|trans_title=Okeanos joins the ranks of LEVIATHAN to achieve qualification to EWC 2025|language={{flag|esmx}} Spanish|author='''Leviatán'''|date=2025-05-14}}</ref><ref name="M80 departure">{{cite web|url=https://x.com/M80gg/status/1922723892805750947|title=Today, Sato & Okeanos have been transferred to a new and exciting oppurtunity|author='''M80'''|date=2025-05-14}}</ref> After these changes, M80 announced that they would be departing Challengers, relinquishing their slot to their players to compete as a free-agent team.<ref name="Chets pets">{{cite web|url=https://x.com/m80gg/status/1923489557397340171|title=M80 VALORANT UPDATE|author='''M80'''|date=2025-05-16}}</ref>

On May 24<sup>th</sup> 2025, M80 announced the release of their final ''VALORANT'' player [[wedid]], ending their time in ''VALORANT'' and disbanding the roster.<ref name="M80 disband">{{cite web|url=https://x.com/M80gg/status/1926396137017167908|title=The Last Standing Member|author='''M80'''|date=2025-05-24}}</ref>

